{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=hardirq-shared-lock; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot. Hunt the interrupt-level analogue of the seed's lock-context invariant: lock objects acquired inside hardirq handler bodies (callbacks registered via request_irq/devm_request_irq, or the non-threaded primary handler of request_threaded_irq) that are also taken with plain spin_lock() rather than spin_lock_irqsave/spin_lock_irq/local_irq_disable from process-context or softirq-context paths (workqueue workers, ioctls, open/close, xmit/NAPI/timer/tasklet callbacks), so the hardirq preempts a holder on the same CPU and spins forever on a lock the preempted context can never release (interrupt-context lockup, watchdog/RCU stall, denial of service). For every candidate record the lock name, the hardirq-side and non-irq-side call chains with file:line, and the missing irq-disable guarantee; the staging ks7010 seed is a demonstration only and must never be reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with candidates plus exact source evidence, or a negative result backed by concrete source evidence."}
